{"step_index":545,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T20:24:01Z","thinking":"**Adding Purchase Option Column**\n\nAdding a new \"Purchase Option\" column to the HTML table will allow displaying purchase actions. Conditional logic in the Javascript file is also needed. The Javascript file needs to verify item availability before rendering a button. The button will only be added to items with a positive stock and that aren't expired.\n\n\n**Implementing Purchase Button Logic**\n\nThe HTML snippet provides the structure for the \"Buy Medicine\" button, including the necessary data attributes. The condition to render \"Out of Stock\" is also in the HTML. Checking the JavaScript file indicates where to incorporate the conditional logic for displaying the appropriate button based on stock and expiry status. Line 230 seems to be in an `availablePharmacies.map` function, which is the right place to build the logic to render either the Buy button or the Out of Stock button.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"C:\\Users\\User\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\medcheck-bd\\client\\history.html","EndLine":173,"StartLine":70,"toolAction":"View history.html script","toolSummary":"View script in client/history.html"}}]}
{"step_index":546,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T20:24:07Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-11T02:24:07+06:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-11T02:24:08+06:00\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/User/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/medcheck-bd/client/history.html`\nTotal Lines: 173\nTotal Bytes: 6360\nShowing lines 70 to 173\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n70: \n71:   <!-- Scripts -->\n72:   <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.3/dist/js/bootstrap.bundle.min.js\"></script>\n73:   <script src=\"js/main.js\"></script>\n74:   <script src=\"js/auth.js\"></script>\n75:   <script>\n76:     document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {\n77:       if (!enforceRoleGuard(['customer', 'admin'])) return;\n78:       loadCustomerHistory();\n79:     });\n80: \n81:     async function loadCustomerHistory() {\n82:       const type = document.getElementById('historyFilter').value;\n83:       const tableBody = document.getElementById('historyTableBody');\n84: \n85:       try {\n86:         const res = await fetch(`/api/history?type=${type}`, { headers: getAuthHeaders() });\n87:         const data = await res.json();\n88: \n89:         if (!res.ok) throw new Error(data.message);\n90: \n91:         const items = data.data || [];\n92:         if (items.length === 0) {\n93:           tableBody.innerHTML = `\n94:             <tr>\n95:               <td colspan=\"8\" class=\"text-center py-5 text-muted\">\n96:                 <i class=\"fas fa-history fa-2x mb-2 d-block opacity-50\"></i>\n97:                 No history entries found. Search and verify medicines to log items here.\n98:               </td>\n99:             </tr>\n100:           `;\n101:           return;\n102:         }\n103: \n104:         tableBody.innerHTML = items.map(item => `\n105:           <tr>\n106:             <td>\n107:               <strong class=\"text-navy\">${item.medicineName}</strong>\n108:               <div class=\"small text-muted\">${item.genericName || ''}</div>\n109:             </td>\n110:             <td>${item.manufacturer || 'N/A'}</td>\n111:             <td class=\"font-monospace small\">${item.batchNumber || 'N/A'}</td>\n112:             <td>\n113:               <span class=\"badge ${item.type === 'PURCHASE' ? 'bg-success' : 'bg-primary'}\">${item.type}</span>\n114:             </td>\n115:             <td>\n116:               <span class=\"status-pill match\">${item.verificationStatus}</span>\n117:             </td>\n118:             <td>${item.pharmacyName || '<span class=\"text-muted small\">MedCheck BD Search</span>'}</td>\n119:             <td class=\"small text-muted\">${formatDate(item.checkedAt)}</td>\n120:             <td class=\"text-end\">\n121:               ${item.medicineId ? `\n122:                 <a href=\"medicine-details.html?id=${item.medicineId._id || item.medicineId}\" class=\"btn btn-outline-primary btn-sm py-0 px-2 me-1\">\n123:                   View\n124:                 </a>\n125:               ` : ''}\n126:               <button class=\"btn btn-outline-danger btn-sm py-0 px-2\" onclick=\"deleteHistoryItem('${item._id}')\">\n127:                 <i class=\"fas fa-trash-alt\"></i>\n128:               </button>\n129:             </td>\n130:           </tr>\n131:         `).join('');\n132:       } catch (err) {\n133:         showToast(err.message, 'danger');\n134:       }\n135:     }\n136: \n137:     async function deleteHistoryItem(id) {\n138:       try {\n139:         const res = await fetch(`/api/history/${id}`, {\n140:           method: 'DELETE',\n141:           headers: getAuthHeaders(),\n142:         });\n143:         const data = await res.json();\n144:         if (!res.ok) throw new Error(data.message);\n145: \n146:         showToast('Record deleted from history', 'info');\n147:         loadCustomerHistory();\n148:       } catch (err) {\n149:         showToast(err.message, 'danger');\n150:       }\n151:     }\n152: \n153:     async function clearAllHistory() {\n154:       if (!confirm('Are you sure you want to clear your entire medicine history?')) return;\n155: \n156:       try {\n157:         const res = await fetch('/api/history', {\n158:           method: 'DELETE',\n159:           headers: getAuthHeaders(),\n160:         });\n161:         const data = await res.json();\n162:         if (!res.ok) throw new Error(data.message);\n163: \n164:         showToast('History cleared successfully', 'info');\n165:         loadCustomerHistory();\n166:       } catch (err) {\n167:         showToast(err.message, 'danger');\n168:       }\n169:     }\n170:   </script>\n171: </body>\n172: </html>\n173: \nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
{"step_index":547,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T20:24:08Z","thinking":"**Improving History Page Resilience**\n\nThe goal is to make the `history.html` page more robust. A critical aspect is handling 401 errors (unauthorized). Upon encountering a 401 status, the stale token should be cleared from storage. An informative alert must be displayed to the user, indicating session expiration or login requirements.\n\n\n**Implementing Session Expiration Handling**\n\nThe provided snippet showcases handling a login session expiration scenario.  A \"1-Click Customer Login\" button is being implemented that triggers an auto-login function, providing a seamless user experience upon session expiration. The auto-login function utilizes an API call to re-authenticate the user, stores the new token, and redirects if authentication fails.\n\n\n**Generating Dynamic Placeholder Content**\n\nHandling different \"no data\" states within the history page, a dynamic approach is needed. Conditional HTML blocks are constructed, each tailored to a specific data type: purchases, verifications, or combined records. The snippet utilizes distinct `<tr>` elements with informative messages and corresponding action links for each condition.\n\nThe logic dynamically renders the correct \"no data\" message and CTA depending on the absence of a certain record type within the page. This approach ensures informative display for the user.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"C:\\Users\\User\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\medcheck-bd\\server\\seed\\seedData.js","EndLine":1425,"StartLine":1375,"toolAction":"View customer history seeding","toolSummary":"View history seeding in seedData.js"}}]}
